## Day 2 — Math LoRA Training (DeepSeek-Math-7B)

**Environment**: Colab Instance #1 (T4/A100 GPU)

### Script: `day2_math_sft.py`

#### Configuration
| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| Base model | `deepseek-ai/deepseek-math-7b-instruct` |
| Quantization | 4-bit NF4 (BitsAndBytes) |
| LoRA rank | 16 |
| LoRA alpha | 32 |
| LoRA target modules | `q_proj, k_proj, v_proj, o_proj, gate_proj, up_proj, down_proj` |
| Learning rate | 2e-4 |
| Batch size | 2 (gradient accumulation 4 → effective 8) |
| Epochs | 3 |
| Max sequence length | 1024 |
| Warmup ratio | 0.05 |
| Optimizer | paged_adamw_8bit |
| Scheduler | cosine |

#### Training Pipeline
1. Mount Google Drive, load `math_train.jsonl` and `math_val.jsonl`
2. Load base model in 4-bit with `BitsAndBytesConfig`
3. Apply LoRA with `peft`
4. Format dataset using tokenizer with ChatML template
5. Train with `SFTTrainer` (from `trl`)
6. Evaluate on validation set every 50 steps
7. Save best adapter to `drive/MyDrive/lora_math/`

#### Outputs
- `drive/MyDrive/lora_math/` — LoRA adapter weights
- `drive/MyDrive/lora_math/training_log.json` — loss curves, eval metrics

